      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "48. We did not acquire untainted knowledge; nor did",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "we amass wealth; we did not even serve our parents with a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "devoted mind; nor did we embrace young women with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "long sparkling eyes even in a dream; like crows we have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "passed this period (of our life ) craving a morsel from others.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "49. Those from whom we were born have long since pas-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "sed away; those too, with whom we grew up, have been",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "consigned to the region of memory; now here we are, with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "our fall approaching nearer and nearer day by day, reduced",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "to the same state as that of trees (growing) on the bank of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "a sandy river.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "50. The life of men is limited to a hundred years;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "half of it passes away in the night; of the remaining half",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "one-half made up of its first and last fourths is occupied by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "youth and old age; the remainder is passed in servitude",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "&c., accompanied by disease and grief for the separation ( of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "relations ). Whence can there be any happiness for mortals",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "in wordly life which is even more unsteady than a wave?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "51. Like an actor, a man for a time plays the child,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "and then for an instant the youth delighting in pleasures;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "for a moment he plays the part of poverty, at another he is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "full of prosperity; and at the close of life he retires behind",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the curtain of Yama’s seat, his limbs wasted by old age, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "his body graced by wrinkles.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "52. You are a king; we too are exalted by the pride we",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "take in the wisdom acquired from the preceptor whom we",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "served; you are known for your greatness, (even) our fame",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the poets spread in all directions; thus, O mortifier ( of men )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the difference between us is not very great; if you turn",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "away your face from us, we too are utterly indifferent",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "( to you ).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "53. You are the lord of riches in full, we too of words in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "all their senses; you are brave, our skill in the act of subduing",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
